  "coverage_interpretation": "348 numeric evidence records. Size-reference coverage is 78 of 136 source identities, leaving 58 gaps. Kathleen gains sampled drifter-axis extrema; Murphy gains two sampled ellipse dimensions, a separately defined baroclinic radius of influence and a definition-unspecified reported diameter. These are not five interchangeable whole-eddy dimensions or a seasonal series. Sixteen entries lack their own numeric evidence.",
  "scope_limits": [
    "Original SAIC Year 5 report acquired; printed pages 110, 123, 174 and 242 visually reviewed. Original assets stay in ignored cache, not republished.",
    "Nowlin et al. explicitly associates Kathleen with E and Murphy with F. Registry physical identity and the differing separation conventions remain unreconciled.",
    "The reported 170-to-50 km drifter-axis decrease does not specify each endpoint separately by major/minor axis or exact dates. It is not a 50–170 km annual or seasonal range.",
    "The source paragraph prints Figure 4.2-26b while the matching caption is Figure 4.3-26b. This discrepancy remains explicit.",
    "The 244 by 148 km ellipse describes Drifter 3345 during mid-July/early August 1988. The source warns that the drifter need not follow the eddy front or one parcel continuously.",
    "The late-August 180 km radius is the baroclinic influence diagnosed from the 8°C temperature surface, not a universal outer radius or velocity-maximum radius.",
    "The 300 km diameter statement lacks a specified boundary and precise observation date. The shedding date does not date the diameter.",
    "No radius doubling, area conversion, inferred diameter lower bound from the 340 km section, whole-lifetime, annual envelope, physical footprint, state containment, runtime or release installation."
  ],
  "full_goal_complete": false
